1
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:12,920
Try stepping back and
looking at it in the light.

2
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:28,600
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out to you.

3
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:35,300
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand.

4
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,420
That strange feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,120 --> 00:00:47,700
So on the arcade guide tiles,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,480
I tried walking only on the black parts.

7
00:00:55,860 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,800
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:09,060
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the blue-shadowed aunties too.

10
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:14,660
Go on, turn that corner over there.

11
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,900
You'll get to meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kame-ari surely Kame-ari!

13
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:32,980
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,060 --> 00:01:34,580
Thank you.

15
00:01:42,480 --> 00:01:45,000
Diary of a Downtown Police Box

16
00:01:51,460 --> 00:01:53,440
Long torso, short legs, bowlegged,

17
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:56,920
smoky all over, wild and fearless.

18
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,680
Is this man really a police officer?

19
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:02,440
He's Patrol Sergeant Kankichi Ryotsu.

20
00:02:03,260 --> 00:02:06,120
He's coming to our police box from
Katsushika Station on temporary duty.

21
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:09,180
So the squad leader came
all the way to pick him up?

22
00:02:09,180 --> 00:02:12,780
We agreed to meet at the east exit at three,
but he still hasn't shown up.

23
00:02:12,780 --> 00:02:16,000
Then he might be waiting at the upper exit.

24
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,600
The east side has two exits, after all.

25
00:02:19,040 --> 00:02:20,260
I'll go take a look.

26
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:22,080
What's going on?

27
00:02:22,080 --> 00:02:22,680
Taaroo!

28
00:02:26,340 --> 00:02:27,720
Watch out! Stop him!

29
00:02:27,800 --> 00:02:27,940
Yes!

30
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,320
Hurry, get away up the stairs!

31
00:02:36,960 --> 00:02:38,280
Stop it! Taro!

32
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:42,840
Yodaru-chan!

33
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,880
Whoa! Scary! Scary! Scary!

34
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:48,900
Dossai!

35
00:02:49,740 --> 00:02:52,020
Wow, amazing! The cop stopped the cow!

36
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:54,800
It's dangerous, so run up to the road above!

37
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:56,800
Squad leader, could it be...

38
00:02:58,020 --> 00:03:01,660
Off the charts, wild, with brute strength...

39
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:04,620
So that guy is Ryotsu!

40
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:06,100
Whoa!

41
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:07,960
Whoa!

42
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:10,180
Ow! What a heavy cow, damn it!

43
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,260
Are you all right?

44
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:15,680
Let me tend to that wound.

45
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:17,820
A scratch like this'll
heal if you just lick it.

46
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:20,640
Who are you, knowing my name?

47
00:03:21,020 --> 00:03:23,220
Squad leader of the
Shitaya Fifth Police Box.

48
00:03:23,220 --> 00:03:24,480
I'm Ban-isoroku.

49
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:26,160
It's good to finally meet you.

50
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,480
I'm Ryotsu, nice to meet you.

51
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,540
You did a fine job right off the bat.

52
00:03:30,980 --> 00:03:33,080
If that wound's fine, shall we get going?

53
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:35,580
Isn't this the police box?

54
00:03:35,800 --> 00:03:36,200
Yeah.

55
00:03:36,200 --> 00:03:37,980
I'll show you the way, so follow me.

56
00:03:37,980 --> 00:03:38,480
Yes.

57
00:03:39,200 --> 00:03:41,840
I hear you know this area well.

58
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:44,040
Well, my family home is nearby, so.

59
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:45,720
It used to be our playground back then.

60
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:48,360
By the way, what's the deal with that cow?

61
00:03:48,360 --> 00:03:51,200
Taro, the one we keep at the police box, and

62
00:03:51,200 --> 00:03:53,400
You keep a cow at the police box?

63
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,980
Well, normally it's quite docile.

64
00:03:55,980 --> 00:03:58,260
No, that's not the point.

65
00:03:58,260 --> 00:03:59,260
Isn't that Rō-san?

66
00:03:59,260 --> 00:04:01,060
It's been a while.

67
00:04:01,060 --> 00:04:03,980
Your father seems to be doing well

68
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:06,520
Good health is his only virtue.

69
00:04:06,520 --> 00:04:08,380
You two know each other?

70
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:11,000
It's my middle school classmate's place.

71
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:14,020
With the downtown boom, the dagashi
shops must be doing great, right?

72
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:15,660
That's not the case at all.

73
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:18,940
Dagashi shops themselves are disappearing in Tokyo,
you know.

74
00:04:18,940 --> 00:04:21,640
The one next door closed up shop last year.

75
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:24,980
Back in the Showa 30s, when dagashi
shops were at their peak after the war,

76
00:04:24,980 --> 00:04:28,980
people came to Nippori from all over Tokyo to buy sweets in bulk,
they did.

77
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:33,400
Back then,
this corner had over 60 dagashi shops too,

78
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:35,980
but now there are fewer than ten left.

79
00:04:36,340 --> 00:04:40,180
Ours is the only one still determined
to keep up the business, though.

80
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:42,340
Cheer up, old man.

81
00:04:42,760 --> 00:04:44,220
Then let's buy two boxes.

82
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:47,040
We'll come back and buy them
all in bulk at the next gathering.

83
00:04:47,360 --> 00:04:48,780
Sorry, Ryo-san.

84
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:52,560
Is this the Shitaya Fifth police box?

85
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:53,640
That's right.

86
00:04:54,040 --> 00:04:55,700
Just like a police box

87
00:04:57,520 --> 00:04:58,920
Hey, what do you think you're doing?

88
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:02,520
Stop it, Ryotsu.

89
00:05:02,780 --> 00:05:04,420
I asked you to mind the place.

90
00:05:04,500 --> 00:05:05,440
To the dog?

91
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:09,340
There, there. You did well, Kankichi.

92
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,180
His name is Kankichi?

93
00:05:12,400 --> 00:05:14,660
You're a Kankichi too, aren't you.

94
00:05:14,660 --> 00:05:16,980
Don't take it the wrong way.
It's just a coincidence.

95
00:05:16,980 --> 00:05:19,100
You all did well too.

96
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:22,500
There are more of them?

97
00:05:22,920 --> 00:05:24,100
Yes, all of them.

98
00:05:24,520 --> 00:05:27,140
There's Reiko, Keiichi, and Daijirō.

99
00:05:27,820 --> 00:05:30,700
A bunch of the same crew as the Kameari lot.

100
00:05:31,440 --> 00:05:33,200
Do you love animals?

101
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:36,340
Well, I kept bringing home strays,

102
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:38,080
and before I knew it,
they just kept multiplying.

103
00:05:38,080 --> 00:05:39,240
Which one is it

104
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,500
You picked up all of these?

105
00:05:42,660 --> 00:05:44,840
It's like an animal kingdom.

106
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,720
Squad leader, did you bring home a kid too?

107
00:05:52,720 --> 00:05:55,240
Idiot, the neighborhood
kids came over to play.

108
00:05:56,420 --> 00:05:59,380
Then, Ryotsu,
you'll be in charge of feeding.

109
00:05:59,380 --> 00:06:00,300
Just as I thought.

110
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:03,420
So who's going to feed us?

111
00:06:04,180 --> 00:06:06,060
Then there's nothing to worry about.

112
00:06:06,060 --> 00:06:07,320
Good evening, Bansar.

113
00:06:07,760 --> 00:06:10,420
Tonight it's oden,
so please help yourself if you like.

114
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:12,740
Mr. Tanaka, I'm always sorry to trouble you.

115
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:15,680
The kids are always being looked after by you,
after all.

116
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,060
And some Usagiya wagashi, too.

117
00:06:18,060 --> 00:06:19,280
I'm terribly sorry.

118
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:22,240
Hey, we're going home, Ichiro and Jiro.

119
00:06:22,240 --> 00:06:22,480
Yes.

120
00:06:23,180 --> 00:06:25,860
We always have plenty from neighbors' gifts.

121
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:26,920
I see.

122
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:29,960
Well then, take care on your way.

123
00:06:29,960 --> 00:06:30,780
Bye-bye.

124
00:06:31,440 --> 00:06:32,160
See you.

125
00:06:33,580 --> 00:06:35,980
Back in the day, people used to be
scared of police boxes, you know.

126
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:38,700
With a police box here,
the parents feel at ease.

127
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,800
Aren't you Gin-san's boy?

128
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:43,820
The lady from Gofuku-ya in Ueno.

129
00:06:44,360 --> 00:06:46,320
So you've been posted to Ueno?

130
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:48,560
No, I'm only here temporarily.

131
00:06:48,560 --> 00:06:51,680
I see. I'd better let the
councilman know right away.

132
00:06:51,680 --> 00:06:53,800
Hey, don't go doing anything unnecessary.

133
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:56,200
Since you went to the trouble,
I'll leave a little more.

134
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:58,280
This one is really delicious.

135
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:00,540
Even though I'm not fond of sweets.

136
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:04,740
Uh-oh, now that I think about it,
a lot of people here know me.

137
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:08,760
In a neighborhood with so many acquaintances,
we can't act carelessly.

138
00:07:09,120 --> 00:07:11,800
I was born in the shitamachi too,
so I know everyone around here.

139
00:07:12,740 --> 00:07:14,580
It feels like I'm back on duty,
just like ages ago.

140
00:07:14,960 --> 00:07:16,420
Somehow, this feels awkward.

141
00:07:20,440 --> 00:07:21,900
Let's eat!

142
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:24,320
Why are these guys eating with us too?

143
00:07:24,920 --> 00:07:27,760
The more the merrier at mealtime,
don't you think?

144
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:29,400
That's not the point, is it?

145
00:07:30,420 --> 00:07:31,820
Hey, that's mine!

146
00:07:31,820 --> 00:07:34,200
Ryotsu, don't pick on the animal!

147
00:07:34,200 --> 00:07:36,720
But it took my side dish!

148
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:41,100
Then why don't you just get
some of Kankichi's dog food?

149
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:45,820
For goodness' sake,
you're such a picky eater.

150
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:49,260
Nobody actually chooses to eat dog food,
you know.

151
00:07:51,080 --> 00:07:54,000
It might be a bit cramped, but bear with it.

152
00:07:54,560 --> 00:07:57,300
That's fine, as long as I get
to sleep on such a nice futon.

153
00:07:58,200 --> 00:07:59,960
Those are Kankichi and the others' futons.

154
00:08:00,660 --> 00:08:02,720
Sorry, yours is over here.

155
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,920
Do I have to share a room with
these guys when I sleep too?

156
00:08:06,480 --> 00:08:07,300
Of course.

157
00:08:07,300 --> 00:08:10,100
Well, I'll come wake
you when your shift's up.

158
00:08:16,380 --> 00:08:18,640
Honestly, what a mess.

159
00:08:21,520 --> 00:08:25,140
You're going to the Shitaya Fifth
police box in Ueno as a substitute?

160
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:29,600
That's right. Five of the six officers came
down with colds and ended up in the hospital.

161
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:34,200
So we need an officer who knows
Ueno well and never catches a cold.

162
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:38,140
After searching,
we concluded that you're the only one.

163
00:08:38,140 --> 00:08:41,540
Being chosen for a temporary transfer,
that's amazing!

164
00:08:42,800 --> 00:08:47,320
You're meeting the squad leader from the Shitaya
Fifth police box at the east exit of Nippori Station.

165
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,340
Right now?

166
00:08:49,340 --> 00:08:54,360
That's right. They say you should throw
your favorite child into a deep valley.

167
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,760
It's "send them on a journey," isn't it?

168
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:59,060
What? What happened?

169
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,360
It's time.

170
00:09:01,360 --> 00:09:03,400
It's still dark.

171
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:06,120
Five in the morning is
feeding time for the birds.

172
00:09:08,260 --> 00:09:12,360
I'm starting to understand why the officers wore
themselves down and ended up in the hospital.

173
00:09:21,380 --> 00:09:23,220
What are you building, Ryotsu?

174
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:25,160
It's a shed to put these guys in.

175
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:28,620
You're going to lock these
animals up in a place like this?

176
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:30,860
This is normal in the real world.

177
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:33,120
The Chief is far too soft on animals.

178
00:09:33,660 --> 00:09:37,060
At this rate,
these guys won't survive the 21st century.

179
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:39,600
I intend to look after that myself.

180
00:09:40,160 --> 00:09:43,220
What if the Chief gets sick
or injured and is hospitalized?

181
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:45,460
Or what if he gets transferred?

182
00:09:45,800 --> 00:09:48,120
Nobody else will look after these guys.

183
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:50,280
W-well, that's...

184
00:09:51,060 --> 00:09:56,620
To prepare for that day, I'm going to teach
these guys how to behave as ordinary pets.

185
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:59,820
Chief, how have you handled
their walks until now?

186
00:09:59,820 --> 00:10:03,260
Well, I've left it up to
the animals' own initiative.

187
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:06,560
And look what that's led to,
look at Daijiro's belly.

188
00:10:06,560 --> 00:10:08,720
It's pure middle-aged paunch.

189
00:10:08,720 --> 00:10:10,700
Don't blame me if he ends up with diabetes.

190
00:10:12,260 --> 00:10:15,920
Starting today, I'm going to whip
these guys into shape thoroughly.

191
00:10:24,520 --> 00:10:26,460
Tanaka Cemetery Brings back memories.

192
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:29,400
We used to hold bonus-prize
contests here when we were kids.

193
00:10:36,280 --> 00:10:39,380
Hey! You're dogs, and you're
messing up over something this small!

194
00:10:42,380 --> 00:10:43,000
Squad Leader!

195
00:10:44,380 --> 00:10:46,000
It's been a real handful.

196
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:47,860
You lot.

197
00:10:47,860 --> 00:10:49,500
It's hopeless.

198
00:10:49,500 --> 00:10:51,520
They don't have even half my stamina.

199
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:55,160
From now on,
I'll take them along on patrols.

200
00:10:57,460 --> 00:10:57,820
Chow time.

201
00:10:59,740 --> 00:11:02,440
And starting today,
that's your sleeping quarters.

202
00:11:02,440 --> 00:11:03,680
Get some rest.

203
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:09,340
Thanks for the food.

204
00:11:13,380 --> 00:11:15,740
Wouldn't it be better to
let them eat a little more?

205
00:11:15,740 --> 00:11:17,640
They've also had some exercise today.

206
00:11:17,640 --> 00:11:18,520
No way.

207
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:20,720
They're already on the chubby side.

208
00:11:20,720 --> 00:11:22,740
We need to put them on a diet, starting now.

209
00:11:48,020 --> 00:11:50,580
Alright, Ryotsu. Time for your shift.

210
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:53,080
How long do you plan on sleeping?

211
00:11:54,120 --> 00:11:54,760
Get up!

212
00:11:54,940 --> 00:11:56,040
Come on, you lot!

213
00:12:07,300 --> 00:12:07,700
What?

214
00:12:08,620 --> 00:12:10,420
Why am I in a place like this?

215
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:13,800
I was definitely sleeping in my futon.

216
00:12:27,180 --> 00:12:28,880
Defying me, of all people, how dare you.

217
00:12:28,880 --> 00:12:30,540
What an outrageous bunch.

218
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:32,200
Your speed is dropping!

219
00:12:32,200 --> 00:12:33,500
Put more spirit into it!

220
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:38,240
Hey.

221
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:40,340
Which way are we going?

222
00:12:44,840 --> 00:12:47,700
Damn it,
this lot's got nothing but sneaky tricks!

223
00:12:56,040 --> 00:12:57,040
I'm back.

224
00:12:57,040 --> 00:12:58,200
There you are. I've been waiting.

225
00:12:59,020 --> 00:13:01,700
Do you know the police box
at the foot of Yushima Tenjin?

226
00:13:01,780 --> 00:13:04,160
The one standing at the intersection, right?

227
00:13:04,160 --> 00:13:06,560
I know you just got back, but...

228
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:08,840
Could you go return the bento boxes there?

229
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:11,080
It's like a kid's errand, isn't it?

230
00:13:11,660 --> 00:13:13,140
You two come along too.

231
00:13:17,320 --> 00:13:19,300
Yanaka really has a lot of temples.

232
00:13:19,300 --> 00:13:22,660
Well, Kan'ei-ji is up on Ueno Hill,
after all.

233
00:13:23,140 --> 00:13:24,300
Ryo-san.

234
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:26,920
Ichiro, Jiro.

235
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:29,700
I was just about to head to the police box.

236
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:32,300
I just can't clear this game no matter what.

237
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:34,380
I'm just running a quick errand.

238
00:13:34,380 --> 00:13:35,780
Wait at the police box.

239
00:13:36,300 --> 00:13:36,700
Yeah.

240
00:13:37,420 --> 00:13:39,140
So you're Ryo-san

241
00:13:39,140 --> 00:13:41,320
You're just like I imagined.

242
00:13:41,320 --> 00:13:42,960
Are you really that famous?

243
00:13:44,800 --> 00:13:47,160
That's right. Even at headquarters,
there's no one who doesn't know him.

244
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:48,480
Here you go.

245
00:13:48,480 --> 00:13:49,340
Thanks.

246
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:53,780
Fine, but just a little.

247
00:13:53,780 --> 00:13:55,220
They'll just get fat again.

248
00:13:58,020 --> 00:14:01,320
There's Shinobazu Pond nearby,
so it's a nice environment, isn't it?

249
00:14:01,780 --> 00:14:04,140
I used to come here to play
all the time when I was a kid.

250
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:06,800
I've come to Yushima
Tenjin a few times, too.

251
00:14:07,300 --> 00:14:09,960
When going all the way to Hongō,
that long slope is tough.

252
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:12,340
There used to be a sake brewery around here,
you know.

253
00:14:12,340 --> 00:14:14,080
Early in the Showa era, I think.

254
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:15,900
Cars were few and far between,

255
00:14:15,900 --> 00:14:19,000
back when handcarts were
how goods got hauled.

256
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:22,340
Right here at the bottom of the slope,
I'd knock back a go of sake.

257
00:14:22,340 --> 00:14:25,220
Then I'd charge straight up
this Kirido slope in one go.

258
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:27,700
Since a handcart's load is heavy,

259
00:14:27,700 --> 00:14:30,380
keeping it from stalling halfway
is where your strength really shows.

260
00:14:31,360 --> 00:14:33,520
You seem well-informed,
but where were you born?

261
00:14:33,520 --> 00:14:34,800
My family's been here for generations.

262
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:36,600
Right near the Yoshiwara Great Gate.

263
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:39,260
Kanda Myojin is close by too.
It's a nice place here.

264
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:43,060
You weren't by any chance carrying a mikoshi at the Kanda Festival,
were you?

265
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:46,640
I always go out for security at the Kanda Festival,
you know.

266
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:50,360
I feel like you look like the
guy who always causes trouble.

267
00:14:52,360 --> 00:14:56,280
Wait, aren't you the cop who's
always trying to arrest me?

268
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:00,020
That must be some kind of mistake.

269
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:02,360
I think your voice sounds similar too.

270
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:04,120
I'm from Asakusa, after all.

271
00:15:04,120 --> 00:15:06,500
I only carry a mikoshi
during the Sanja Festival.

272
00:15:06,500 --> 00:15:08,660
Well, I suppose it's
about time to head home.

273
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:09,920
Wait a second.

274
00:15:12,060 --> 00:15:13,620
W-what is it?

275
00:15:14,520 --> 00:15:18,080
Could you deliver this pot to
the Hongō Tōdai-mae police box?

276
00:15:21,740 --> 00:15:23,720
Sorry to trouble you, officer.

277
00:15:23,720 --> 00:15:25,740
Looks like I'll have business
to take care of in Hongō.

278
00:15:25,740 --> 00:15:27,360
I'll climb up with you.

279
00:15:29,760 --> 00:15:31,940
What's wrong with you lot?
Pull yourselves together!

280
00:15:32,380 --> 00:15:34,340
You still need more training.

281
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:38,960
Don't go wandering around like an idiot,
Kankichi.

282
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:42,000
Just as expected of
someone who shares my name.

283
00:15:42,760 --> 00:15:45,000
Are you Ryotsu from the Katsushika station?

284
00:15:45,840 --> 00:15:47,220
I've heard all sorts of rumors about you.

285
00:15:47,940 --> 00:15:49,080
What kind of rumors?

286
00:15:49,680 --> 00:15:50,500
There are plenty of them.

287
00:15:50,940 --> 00:15:52,340
They say he punched the chief.

288
00:15:52,340 --> 00:15:54,460
And that he drove twenty patrol cars around.

289
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:56,620
So those rumors are true

290
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,340
You're back?

291
00:15:58,640 --> 00:15:59,940
He came by to deliver the pot.

292
00:16:00,280 --> 00:16:02,780
He's currently on loan to
the Shitaya Fifth police box.

293
00:16:02,780 --> 00:16:04,000
It's Senior Officer Ryotsu.

294
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:06,000
That famous one?

295
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,640
You're the guy who set a
police box on fire, right?

296
00:16:08,640 --> 00:16:09,940
I know him well.

297
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:10,920
No, that's not right.

298
00:16:10,920 --> 00:16:13,940
Ryo-san became famous for
blowing up headquarters.

299
00:16:13,940 --> 00:16:16,000
That was the Katsushika
station bombing, right?

300
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:17,720
The one where he blew up headquarters -

301
00:16:17,720 --> 00:16:20,540
Squad leader, let's leave it at that.

302
00:16:21,200 --> 00:16:21,560
Yeah, yeah.

303
00:16:22,100 --> 00:16:24,300
I hear you know this area well.

304
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:26,960
This area's like my own backyard.

305
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:30,280
When I was a kid,
I'd fish at Sanshiro Pond at Todai,

306
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:33,300
and run around inside Yasuda Auditorium.

307
00:16:34,200 --> 00:16:36,620
Our chief's pretty clueless about geography,
you know.

308
00:16:37,080 --> 00:16:39,620
You've got to learn it on your own two feet.

309
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:42,300
Just past the slope down from
the Hongō Yayoi intersection,

310
00:16:42,300 --> 00:16:43,840
there's a police box. Did you know that?

311
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:45,000
Of course.

312
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:47,360
Go return the sukiyaki pot there.

313
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,680
You're going that way anyway, right?

314
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:49,760
Yeah.

315
00:16:50,160 --> 00:16:53,580
And return the TV we borrowed from the
Dangozaka Shita Minami police box in Sendagi, too.

316
00:16:54,120 --> 00:16:54,760
Right.

317
00:16:54,760 --> 00:16:57,040
It's a bit far,
but you've got a bicycle, so it's fine.

318
00:16:57,660 --> 00:16:59,860
Mistaking me for a delivery service,

319
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:03,500
take four of those as souvenirs.

320
00:17:05,200 --> 00:17:06,620
Here you go, sorry for the wait.

321
00:17:06,620 --> 00:17:08,640
You've got to chill them well before eating.

322
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:09,940
I know.

323
00:17:09,940 --> 00:17:13,720
We've gotten so late, haven't we.

324
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:15,460
These are souvenirs for
Ichirō and the others.

325
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:16,820
Let's go, you guys!

326
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,660
Can't be helped

327
00:17:22,100 --> 00:17:23,440
It should be around here somewhere.

328
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:25,420
Here, drink up.

329
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:27,020
That'll perk you right up.

330
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,520
Was this your first time having ramune?

331
00:17:33,180 --> 00:17:35,520
Alright, alright,
I'll let you drink the whole thing.

332
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:37,220
Once you've finished, we're heading out.

333
00:17:40,680 --> 00:17:41,680
You're slow, Ryotsu.

334
00:17:42,020 --> 00:17:44,940
I suppose I should head off to
the squad leaders' meeting soon.

335
00:17:48,460 --> 00:17:49,420
Can't be helped.

336
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:54,560
I'm leaving the rest to you, all right?

337
00:17:55,700 --> 00:17:56,180
Yes, let's go.

338
00:17:57,700 --> 00:18:01,700
The suspect is fleeing
northbound along Nikkō Kaidō.

339
00:18:09,980 --> 00:18:11,340
It stinks!

340
00:18:25,200 --> 00:18:26,480
W-why is there a cow?!

341
00:18:27,720 --> 00:18:29,000
What is this outbreak?!

342
00:18:45,280 --> 00:18:46,760
Isato, this way!

343
00:18:47,820 --> 00:18:49,660
Everyone! There are hostages!

344
00:18:53,220 --> 00:18:53,540
Yes.

345
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:56,520
The culprit is at the
Kitaya Fifth Police Box,

346
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:57,080
Rojo Middle School.

347
00:18:58,080 --> 00:18:59,400
It's my senior's police box.

348
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:09,840
Hey, hey, what are you going to do?

349
00:19:10,280 --> 00:19:10,860
What's the situation?

350
00:19:11,260 --> 00:19:13,660
The culprit wants a helicopter

351
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:14,300
for his getaway.

352
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:17,740
He says that if we don't comply,
he'll harm the children.

353
00:19:18,460 --> 00:19:19,280
How careless of me.

354
00:19:19,620 --> 00:19:21,520
I should have sent the kids home

355
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:22,500
before going out.

356
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:24,620
What's all this commotion?

357
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:25,760
Senpai!

358
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:26,700
Ryo-chan!

359
00:19:27,160 --> 00:19:28,640
What are you two doing here?

360
00:19:29,260 --> 00:19:32,360
The bank robber from
Kameari fled all the way here

361
00:19:32,360 --> 00:19:35,920
and he's holed up inside the police
box with the children as hostages.

362
00:19:36,280 --> 00:19:38,460
What? Then Ichiro and Jiro

363
00:19:39,100 --> 00:19:40,640
have been taken hostage too?

364
00:19:40,980 --> 00:19:41,660
For crying out loud!

365
00:19:42,600 --> 00:19:43,680
Are you ready yet?

366
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:47,240
We're getting ready now.
Just give us a little more time.

367
00:19:47,700 --> 00:19:50,740
Hurry up, or don't blame me if
those brats end up getting hurt.

368
00:19:51,740 --> 00:19:54,360
Jiro! Jiro! Someone save our boys!

369
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:56,500
R-right. I'll hurry them up!

370
00:19:57,580 --> 00:19:59,560
They were waiting for me.

371
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:09,060
Hey! Where are you going?

372
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:15,240
Where is this?

373
00:20:24,520 --> 00:20:25,860
So this is what was here.

374
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:27,680
Enough with the area.

375
00:20:28,180 --> 00:20:29,780
Pull the car up front, ready to go.

376
00:20:29,780 --> 00:20:31,560
Keep the engine running.

377
00:20:31,560 --> 00:20:34,800
We have no choice.
The hostages' lives come first.

378
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:42,100
At this rate, he'll get away.

379
00:20:46,260 --> 00:20:47,640
You don't mean you two...

380
00:20:50,280 --> 00:20:50,900
Got it.

381
00:20:53,460 --> 00:20:54,720
Hey, get up!

382
00:20:55,820 --> 00:20:56,300
Who's there!

383
00:20:58,880 --> 00:20:59,840
What, a dog?

384
00:21:06,060 --> 00:21:07,760
Don't you dare mock me!

385
00:21:12,480 --> 00:21:13,100
Damn it!

386
00:21:17,760 --> 00:21:19,600
Are you alright, Ichiro, Jiro!

387
00:21:19,600 --> 00:21:20,240
Ryo-san!

388
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:26,280
Aaaaah! Don't let that guy get away!

389
00:21:26,280 --> 00:21:27,560
Let's do it, go!

390
00:21:27,560 --> 00:21:31,980
Come on!

391
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:45,000
Taro, the middle one's the great king, yeah.

392
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:45,740
Mm.

393
00:21:51,660 --> 00:21:53,100
Thanks, Kankichi.

394
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:02,940
It was a short time, but thank you so much.

395
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:06,760
I had quite a good time too.

396
00:22:07,560 --> 00:22:08,880
You two take care of yourselves too.

397
00:22:12,080 --> 00:22:13,660
Senpai, it's about time.

398
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,660
Well then, I'll be taking my leave.

399
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:21,220
How was it, senpai?

400
00:22:21,220 --> 00:22:22,900
Working in your hometown...

401
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:24,560
Yeah.

402
00:22:43,660 --> 00:22:50,820
That person is smiling
with an innocent face,

403
00:22:51,960 --> 00:22:58,420
like a child who knows no suffering.

404
00:22:59,840 --> 00:23:07,720
Even if the two of us part ways like this,

405
00:23:07,720 --> 00:23:10,600
wasn't it a little more painful?

406
00:23:11,260 --> 00:23:13,840
I want nothing to do with a place
that stinks of animals like that.

407
00:23:18,460 --> 00:23:19,340
Kankichi

408
00:23:19,340 --> 00:23:26,120
Kankichi

409
00:23:30,020 --> 00:23:33,020
Take care, I'll come visit again.

410
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:42,500
Huh?

411
00:23:43,820 --> 00:23:44,720
Senpai?

412
00:23:46,660 --> 00:23:49,520
Let's go home!
My big brother is waiting for me!

413
00:23:49,940 --> 00:23:50,420
Yes!

414
00:24:11,600 --> 00:24:13,860
Dash, dash, dash

415
00:24:13,860 --> 00:24:19,640
Packed train, catching a nap on Dad's back

416
00:24:20,500 --> 00:24:25,820
Another tough week, and those unreasonable demands,
quite understandable

417
00:24:26,900 --> 00:24:30,520
Baguette in one hand, looking all composed

418
00:24:30,520 --> 00:24:33,320
Beef bowl, extra sauce, cloudy skies

419
00:24:33,320 --> 00:24:36,580
The irritation from endless overtime

420
00:24:36,580 --> 00:24:40,220
Irritation, cleared away in a flash

421
00:24:43,520 --> 00:24:49,980
Every day's a no-problem brain,
once I step under a hot shower

422
00:24:49,980 --> 00:24:56,560
Every day's a no-problem brain,
a sleep pillow restores my energy

423
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:06,180
Every day's a no-problem brain,
I love someone like me

424
00:25:06,180 --> 00:25:09,040
Every day is no problem,

425
00:25:09,040 --> 00:25:12,980
a Monday with hearts flying around.

426
00:25:12,980 --> 00:25:16,400
Undex, Undex, no problem!

427
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:22,880
Sasaki Kojiro of Shibamata Police Station,

428
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:25,800
whoever he is, the kendo tournament champion

429
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:27,860
is surely going to be us,
Katsushika Police Station!

430
00:25:27,860 --> 00:25:31,060
What? A duel at Ganryujima, he says?

431
00:25:31,400 --> 00:25:33,720
Interesting! Let's take him on!

432
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:37,260
Next time: Kendo Ittchokusen, see you then!

433
00:25:38,240 --> 00:25:40,440
That place is Kameari.

434
00:25:41,420 --> 00:25:43,920
Well, surely it's Kameari.

435
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:49,140
Everyone, come visit our town!

436
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:50,720
Thank you.

